[32.812641, "o", "JFIF\r\nExif\r\n75MPix XXXXL size panorama of Mount Ama Dablam - probably the most beautiful peak in Himalayas. \r\n This panoramic landscape is an very high resolution multi-frame composite and is suitable for large scale printing\r\nAma Dablam is a mountain in the Himalaya range of eastern Nepal. The main peak is 6,812  metres, the lower western peak is 5,563 metres. Ama Dablam means  'Mother's neclace'; the long ridges on each side like the arms of a mother (ama) protecting  her child, and the hanging glacier thought of as the dablam, the traditional double-pendant  containing pictures of the gods, worn by Sherpa women. For several days, Ama Dablam dominates  the eastern sky for anyone trekking to Mount Everest basecamp,\r\nhttp://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/\r\n<?xpacket begin=\"\r\n\" id=\"W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d\"?>\r\n<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x=\"adobe:ns:meta/\">\r\n\t<rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\">\r\n\t\t<rdf:Description rdf:about=\"\" xmlns:photoshop=\"http://ns.adobe.com/photoshop/1.0/\" xmlns:Iptc4xmpCore=\"ht"]
[32.812697, "o", "tp://iptc.org/std/Iptc4xmpCore/1.0/xmlns/\"   xmlns:GettyImagesGIFT=\"http://xmp.gettyimages.com/gift/1.0/\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\" xmlns:plus=\"http://ns.useplus.org/ldf/xmp/1.0/\"  xmlns:iptcExt=\"http://iptc.org/std/Iptc4xmpExt/2008-02-29/\" xmlns:xmpRights=\"http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/rights/\" photoshop:Credit=\"Getty Images\" GettyImagesGIFT:AssetID=\"1341288649\" xmpRights:WebStatement=\"https://www.istockphoto.com/legal/license-agreement?utm_medium=organic&amp;utm_source=google&amp;utm_campaign=iptcurl\" >\r\n<dc:creator><rdf:Seq><rdf:li>hadynyah</rdf:li></rdf:Seq></dc:creator><dc:description><rdf:Alt><rdf:li xml:lang=\"x-default\">75MPix XXXXL size panorama of Mount Ama Dablam - probably the most beautiful peak in Himalayas. \r\n This panoramic landscape is an very high resolution multi-frame composite and is suitable for large scale printing\r\nAma Dablam is a mountain in the Himalaya range of eastern Nepal. The main peak is 6,812  metres, the lower western peak is 5,563 metres. Ama Dablam means  &ap"]
[32.812836, "o", "os;Mother&apos;s neclace&apos;; the long ridges on each side like the arms of a mother (ama) protecting  her child, and the hanging glacier thought of as the dablam, the traditional double-pendant  containing pictures of the gods, worn by Sherpa women. For several days, Ama Dablam dominates  the eastern sky for anyone trekking to Mount Everest basecamp</rdf:li></rdf:Alt></dc:description>\r\n<plus:Licensor><rdf:Seq><rdf:li rdf:parseType='Resource'><plus:LicensorURL>https://www.istockphoto.com/photo/license-gm1341288649-?utm_medium=organic&amp;utm_source=google&amp;utm_campaign=iptcurl</plus:LicensorURL></rdf:li></rdf:Seq></plus:Licensor>\r\n\t\t</rdf:Description>\r\n\t</rdf:RDF>\r\n</x:xmpmeta>\r\n<?xpacket end=\"w\"?>\r\nPhotoshop 3.0\r\n8BIM\r\nhadynyah\r\n75MPix XXXXL size panorama of Mount Ama Dablam - probably the most beautiful peak in Himalayas. \r\n This panoramic landscape is an very high resolution multi-frame composite and is suitable for large scale printing\r\nAma Dablam is a mountain in the Himalaya range of eastern Nepal."]
